@startuml components_async_event_delivery
!include ../../../design/theme.iuml

title Async Event Delivery Components

package "Core command path" {
  component "Pipeline / server\n(event producers)" as Producer
  component "Interest checks\n(type/class masks)" as Masks
}

package "Server event layer" {
  component "Event Bus" as Bus
  database "Replay Ring\nbounded FIFO + replay.gap" as Ring
  component "Plugin Event Bridge\nfilter + enqueue" as Bridge
}

package "Runtime log layer" {
  component "pkg/logcollector" as LogCollector
  component "RuntimeLogBatchEventV1\nruntime.logs" as LogBatch
}

package "Plugin routing" {
  queue "Critical traffic\nRPC/hooks/evaluators" as CriticalQ
  queue "Best-effort telemetry\nevents + runtime.logs" as EventQ
  component "PluginConn writer" as Writer
  component "GCPC transport\nUDS + protobuf" as Transport
}

package "IPC plugin process" {
  component "Plugin SDK\nevent dispatcher" as SDK
  component "instrumentation\nOTLP traces/logs" as Instrumentation
  component "Prometheus\nquery-only metrics" as Prometheus
}

Producer --> Masks : ask before building optional data
Masks --> Bus : emit requested operation event
LogCollector --> LogBatch : parse + buffer + periodic flush
LogBatch --> Bus : emit batched diagnostics
Bus --> Ring : retain replayable classes
Bus --> Bridge : live subscriber callback
Bridge --> EventQ : operation.started\noperation.completed\nruntime.logs\nreplay.gap
CriticalQ --> Writer
EventQ --> Writer
Writer --> Transport : serialized GCPC frames
Transport --> SDK
SDK --> Instrumentation : HandleEvent(batch records)
Prometheus ..> Producer : server:query:metrics.commands\n(no event subscription)

note right of Producer
Events are observational.
They cannot deny or mutate command results.
end note

note right of EventQ
Overflow is allowed only for async telemetry
and must increment visible drop/lag/gap counters.
end note

note bottom of LogCollector
Current slice keeps the existing collector path.
Do not show Unix-socket/yamux log transport here.
end note

@enduml
